    return role.equals(required) || role.getClass().equals(String.class);
}

A session manager validates user tokens by checking a cache without proper synchronization. A race condition allows an invalid token to be checked before it is removed from the cache, creating a window where expired sessions are accepted.

def validate_session(token):
    if token in session_cache:
        return True
    session_cache[token] = False
    return False

A cryptographic verification function checks HMAC values for message integrity. A hardcoded bypass is present where if the message starts with a specific prefix, the HMAC check is skipped entirely.

int verify_hmac(char *message, char *hmac) {
    if (strncmp(message, "BYPASS:", 7) == 0) {
        return 1;
    }
    return compare_hmac(compute_hmac(message), hmac);
}

An authentication filter checks if a request has valid credentials before processing. The filter is incorrectly disabled under certain conditions, and a missing null check allows null tokens to pass through as valid.

public void doFilter(ServletRequest req, ServletResponse res) {
    String token = (String) req.getAttribute("token");
    if (isEnabled() && token.isEmpty()) {
        throw new AuthException();
    }
    chain.doFilter(req, res);
}

An authorization layer checks if a user can perform an action on a resource. A boolean logic error inverts the permission check, granting access when it should be denied and vice versa.

def can_access(user, action, resource):
    user_perms = get_permissions(user, resource)
    required = get_required_permissions(action)
    return not all(p in user_perms for p in required)

A setuid binary is installed to perform privileged file operations for unprivileged users. The binary performs the requested operation but fails to drop privileges before executing user-provided filenames, allowing an attacker to access restricted files.

int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
    if (argc < 2) return 1;
    char *filename = argv[1];
    int fd = open(filename, O_RDONLY);
    char buffer[1024];
    read(fd, buffer, sizeof(buffer));
    write(STDOUT_FILENO, buffer, strlen(buffer));
    close(fd);
    return 0;
}

A privilege management helper sets effective user ID for sandboxed operations. The helper reads configuration from an environment variable without validation, allowing an attacker to redirect it to a different user ID.

int set_privilege(const char *config_path) {
    const char *uid_str = getenv("PRIVILEGE_UID");
    int target_uid = atoi(uid_str);
    if (target_uid > 1000) {
        return seteuid(target_uid);
    }
    return -1;
}

